-- An @nlg written on a GIVEN item of a rule written as clauses is attached, as
-- it is on a rule written as one definition (refutation of
-- legalese/l4-ide#545's review, round 4). It used to be reported as not
-- attached: the head form of a group held a copy of each GIVEN input, with
-- the GIVEN's location, and took what was written around the head instead.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour @nlg the colour %c%
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the code of %c%
DECIDE grouped Red IS 1
DECIDE grouped c IS 2

GIVEN c IS A Colour @nlg the colour %c%
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the code of %c%
DECIDE single c IS 1

#EVAL grouped Red
#EVAL single Red
